WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.762
Two useful methods for readable workflows are query and assign.

00:00:04.762 --> 00:00:07.977
Query is another way to filter rows.

00:00:07.977 --> 00:00:16.027
Instead of writing a Boolean expression inside square brackets, you can often write the condition as a readable

00:00:16.027 --> 00:00:21.012
expression. In this example, we keep Web orders with an amount of at least fifty.

00:00:21.012 --> 00:00:28.602
Assign creates a new column and returns a new Data frame, which makes it convenient inside a method chain.

00:00:28.602 --> 00:00:32.671
Here, we calculate a tax value based on the amount.

00:00:33.376 --> 00:00:37.703
These methods are not automatically better than every other Pandas style.

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:39.948
The important goal is clarity.

00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:46.053
If regular bracket filtering is easier to understand for a particular condition, use it.

00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:50.528
If query makes the condition easier to read, use query.

00:00:50.528 --> 00:00:53.168
Run the code and inspect the result.

00:00:53.168 --> 00:00:57.463
Then change Web to Store, or change the minimum amount.

00:00:57.463 --> 00:01:03.992
Small experiments like this are a good way to understand exactly how each condition affects the Data frame.
